# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even in a Windows working tree.
#
# Added 2026-08-30 after a real failure. tools/linuxProvision.sh is
# COPIED to a Linux compute node straight from this working tree, and a
# Windows checkout had rewritten it with CRLF. bash then died on the
# first brace group it met:
#
#   /home/steve/provision.sh: line 88: syntax error near unexpected
#   token `||'
#
# The committed blob was fine - LF, as it should be - so nothing was
# wrong in the repository, and cloning on Linux always worked. The
# corruption happened on checkout, which makes it invisible in a diff
# and easy to misdiagnose as a bug in the script. Pinning eol=lf stops
# the conversion for the files that can never tolerate it.
*.sh text eol=lf
